---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Periscope';
const description =
  'Privacy policy for periscope.surdu.de, covering what data is collected when you join the waitlist and how it is processed under the GDPR.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-500">
      Legal
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-950 md:text-4xl">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-500">
      Plain language first, formal text below. Information per Art. 13 and 14 GDPR.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-zinc-700">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">Short version</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            If you submit your email to the waitlist, it goes to Tally (an
            EU-based form provider) and to me. That is the only personal data
            this site collects from you directly.
          </li>
          <li>
            I will email you once when audits open up, and not again unless you
            ask.
          </li>
          <li>
            No analytics, no tracking pixels, no advertising cookies. The site
            itself sets no cookies for tracking.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can ask me at any time to delete your email. One message to
            <a href="mailto:periscope@surdu.eu" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-zinc-950">periscope@surdu.eu</a>
            is enough.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">1. Controller</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Razvan Andrei Surdu<br />
          [STREET AND HOUSE NUMBER]<br />
          [POSTAL CODE] [CITY], Germany<br />
          Email:
          <a href="mailto:periscope@surdu.eu" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-zinc-950">periscope@surdu.eu</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">
          2. What data is processed and why
        </h2>
        <h3 class="mt-3 font-semibold text-zinc-950">2.1 Waitlist signup</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          When you submit your email through the waitlist form on this page,
          the following is processed:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>your email address;</li>
          <li>
            a non-personal source tag indicating which CTA you used (e.g.
            "hero" or "repeat");
          </li>
          <li>submission timestamp.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-950">Purpose:</strong>
          to notify you once when Periscope audits open up.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-950">Legal basis:</strong>
          Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR (consent, given by submitting the form).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-950">Retention:</strong>
          until you withdraw consent, or until the waitlist purpose is no
          longer relevant (whichever comes first), at which point the address
          is deleted.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-zinc-950">2.2 Server logs</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub Inc. processes standard
          server logs (including IP address, timestamp, user agent, requested
          URL) for the purpose of operating, securing, and protecting the
          service.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-950">Legal basis:</strong>
          Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (legitimate interest in operating a stable and
          secure website).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">3. Recipients and processors</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Personal data is shared with the following processors strictly to
          deliver the service described above:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-950">Tally Forms BV</strong>,
            Belgium. Form provider that captures and stores waitlist
            submissions. EU-based, GDPR-compliant, DPA in place. See
            <a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-zinc-950" rel="noopener">Tally's privacy policy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-950">GitHub, Inc.</strong>,
            88 Colin P Kelly Jr Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. Hosting
            provider for static site delivery. Cross-border transfer is covered
            by the EU&ndash;U.S. Data Privacy Framework. See
            <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-zinc-950" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="font-semibold text-zinc-950">INWX GmbH &amp; Co. KG</strong>,
            domain registrar for surdu.de.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">4. Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          This site sets no cookies for analytics, advertising, or tracking.
          No third-party analytics tools are loaded.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
          The Tally embed may set strictly necessary, functional cookies or
          local storage entries to support form interaction (e.g. preventing
          duplicate submission). These are exempt from consent under § 25 (2)
          TTDSG / TDDDG.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">5. Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Under the GDPR you have the right to:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>access your personal data (Art. 15);</li>
          <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16);</li>
          <li>have your data erased (Art. 17);</li>
          <li>restrict processing (Art. 18);</li>
          <li>data portability (Art. 20);</li>
          <li>object to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21);</li>
          <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing (Art. 7 (3)).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          To exercise any of these, email
          <a href="mailto:periscope@surdu.eu" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-zinc-950">periscope@surdu.eu</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection
          supervisory authority. The competent authority for this site is
          [INSERT THE COMPETENT GERMAN STATE AUTHORITY FOR YOUR RESIDENCE,
          e.g. Berlin: Berliner Beauftragte f&uuml;r Datenschutz und
          Informationsfreiheit].
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">6. International transfers</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Personal data submitted to the waitlist is processed within the EU
          by Tally Forms BV. Hosting via GitHub Pages may involve transfer to
          the United States; this transfer is covered by the
          EU&ndash;U.S. Data Privacy Framework, to which GitHub Inc. is
          certified.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">7. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          This policy may be updated as the site evolves (for example, when
          an email service provider is added). The current version is always
          available at this URL. Material changes will be reflected in the
          "Last updated" date below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">Last updated: [YYYY-MM-DD]</p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm">
      <a href="/" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-zinc-950">
        &larr; Back to Periscope
      </a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
